# while loop exits through break

Verifies `break` terminates the enclosing `while` loop immediately, so the
counter stops producing output once it reaches the sentinel value.

>>> source
let i: int = 0

while (true) {
    if (i == 3) {
        break
    }

    print(i)
    i = i + 1
}

<<< stdout
0
1
2

<<< stderr
